nkage to the NRAMP1 region</article-title><source>Genes Immun</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>104</fpage><lpage>109</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12618857</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b011"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mohamed</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ibrahim</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>EN</given-names></name><name><surname>Peacock</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Khalil</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Genetic susceptibility to visceral leishmaniasis in The Sudan: Linkage and association with <italic>IL4</italic> and <italic>IFNGR1</italic></article-title><source>Genes Immun</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>355</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12847550</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b012"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mohamed</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ibrahim</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>EN</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Cordell</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title><italic>SLC11A1</italic> (formerly <italic>NRAMP1</italic>) and susceptibility to visceral leishmaniasis in The Sudan</article-title><source>Eur J Hum Genet</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>66</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14523377</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b013"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bucheton</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Abel</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>El-Safi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kheir</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pavek</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>A major susceptibility locus on Chromosome 22q12 plays a critical role in the control of kala-azar</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><volume>73</volume><fpage>1052</fpage><lpage>1060</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14557985</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b014"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lander</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kruglyak</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>Genetic dissection of complex traits: Guidelines for interpreting and reporting linkage results</article-title><source>Nat Genet</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>241</fpage><lpage>247</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7581446</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b015"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sawcer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>HB</given-names></name><name><surname>Feakes</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Smaldon</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>A genome screen in multiple sclerosis reveals susceptibility loci on Chromosome 6p21 and 17q22 &#x0005b;see Comment&#x0005d;</article-title><source>Nat Genet</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>464</fpage><lpage>468</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8696343</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b016"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sun</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilder</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>McPeek</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Enhanced pedigree error detection</article-title><source>Hum Hered</source><volume>54</volume><fpage>99</fpage><lpage>110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12566741</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b017"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Risch</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>Assessing the role of HLA-linked and unlinked determinants of disease</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><volume>40</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3468804</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b018"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Siddiqui</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Meisner</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Tosh</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Balakrishnan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghei</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>A major susceptibility locus for leprosy in India maps to Chromosome 10p13</article-title><source>Nat Genet</source><volume>27</volume><fpage>439</fpage><lpage>441</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11279529</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b019"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mira</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Alcais</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Thuc</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Thai</surname><given-names>VH</given-names></name><name><surname>Huong</surname><given-names>NT</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Chromosome 6q25 is linked to susceptibility to leprosy in a Vietnamese population</article-title><source>Nat Genet</source><volume>33</volume><fpage>412</fpage><lpage>415</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12577057</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b020"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Underhill</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Passarino</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Shen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mirazon Lahr</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>The phylogeography of Y chromosome binary haplotypes and the origins of modern human populations</article-title><source>Ann Hum Genet</source><volume>65</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11415522</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b021"><citation citation-type="journal"><year>2002</year><article-title>A nomenclature system for the tree of human Y-chromosomal binary haplogroups</article-title><source>Genome Res</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>339</fpage><lpage>348</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11827954</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pgen-0030071-b022"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leutenegger</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Genin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Clerget-Darpoux</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Impact of parental relationships in maximum lod score affected sib-pair method</article-title><source>Genet Epidemiol</source><volume>23</volume><fpage>413</fpage><lpage>425</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12432507</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pg